# ADR-001: Use Redis for refresh token storage

## Context
JWTs are stateless, so access-token revocation is not immediate unless every
request checks a denylist. The system needs revocable refresh tokens for logout
and to prevent suspended accounts from obtaining new access tokens.

## Decision
Store refresh tokens in Redis with TTL, not in PostgreSQL.

## Consequences
+ Refresh-token revocation is O(1) — just delete the Redis key
+ Suspended accounts cannot get new tokens when they next try to refresh
+ Access tokens already issued remain valid until expiry (15 minutes by default)
- Adds Redis as a required infrastructure dependency
- If Redis goes down, all users are logged out